{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4b7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07d5e-0f16-71a3-abaf-54c2f5d26492"},"sequence":182,"recorded_at":1780531400000359,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf"},"call_id":"call_01a07d5e78e47181a81816cfdd3769d0","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-8-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-1r9wrr) { full }' 2>&1 | head -250\",\n  \"description\": \"Get full task details\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"ac\\\":\\\"Production behavior demonstrates: Derive all SessionState values, winning epochs, conflicts, current checkpoints, provider identity, and terminal binding. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\\\",\\\"assignee\\\":\\\"[implementer] developer (muse)\\\",\\\"blockedBy\\\":[\\\"TASK-260830-wbpf1v\\\"],\\\"blocks\\\":[\\\"TASK-260830-21gygk\\\"],\\\"checklist\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Derive all SessionState values, winning epochs, conflicts, current checkpoints, provider identity, and terminal binding\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every SessionState value is derived from a production path, and the state space is censused rather than listed: a value with no producing path and a path producing an uncensused value both fail\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Winning-epoch resolution is driven at the tie and the gap, not only the clear win; a conflict where both sides are individually valid is refused or resolved by a named rule\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"The reducer is proven pure: the same event sequence yields the same state, and a chain-forbidden reordering does not silently yield a different one\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A parked session from sessrepo reaches SessionState as a state carrying its blocking reason and retry, not as an error or an omission\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Crash and idempotency evidence is produced through secconftest crash points placed inside the durable window, one per step boundary\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every census derives its denominator from production through invcore and fails closed on an unregistered site, an orphan row and an unclassifiable site, each control-planted including an import alias and a var binding\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Mutation battery covers the read and recovery paths as well as the write path, reported killed over applied on a production-derived denominator with narrowing, arm-deletion, census-only and audit-only separate\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every published number is re-derived after the last artifact; candidate tree OID equals the record's by detached-index write-tree and the outcome enumerates exactly the CR changed paths\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Lint clean\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\\"done\\\":false},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\\"done\\\":false}],\\\"children\\\":[],\\\"created\\\":\\\"2026-08-29T22:00:11Z\\\",\\\"derivedBlockedBy\\\":[],\\\"derivedBlocks\\\":[],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Derive all SessionState values, winning epochs, conflicts, current checkpoints, provider identity, and terminal binding. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\\\",\\\"estimate\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"estimated\\\",\\\"scale\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fibonacci\\\",\\\"number\\\":8}},\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1r9wrr\\\",\\\"integrationCheckpointed\\\":false,\\\"isAdvisoryBlocked\\\":false,\\\"isBlocked\\\":false,\\\"name\\\":\\\"implement-session-state-reducer\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"spawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=muse/muse-spark/xhigh pair_source=explicit match=not_recommended snapshot=sha256:08c5d671a0c9e2350b1b8c97c08841f378392d0f4ac8edf05ecf155d29ae97bb rationale=\\\\\\\"implementation class rank 1; second chain leaf, first consumer of leaf 1's per-session parked channel\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: muse via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=muse; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260907-a6765b, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260907-a6765b)\\\",\\\"observability\\\":{\\\"readiness\\\":{\\\"advisoryBlockedElementIds\\\":[],\\\"blockedElementIds\\\":[],\\\"coverage\\\":{\\\"complete\\\":true,\\\"estimated\\\":1,\\\"ratio\\\":\\\"1/1\\\",\\\"total\\\":1,\\\"unestimated\\\":0},\\\"estimateKind\\\":\\\"estimated\\\",\\\"isAdvisoryBlocked\\\":false,\\\"isBlocked\\\":false,\\\"rolledEstimate\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"estimated\\\",\\\"scale\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fibonacci\\\",\\\"number\\\":8}}},\\\"scope\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1r9wrr\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"implement-session-state-reducer\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"task\\\"},\\\"summary\\\":{\\\"active\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1r9wrr\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"implement-session-state-reducer\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"development\\\"}],\\\"blocked\\\":[],\\\"byType\\\":{\\\"bug\\\":{\\\"total\\\":0,\\\"todo\\\":0,\\\"active\\\":0,\\\"done\\\":0,\\\"closed\\\":0,\\\"blocked\\\":0},\\\"epic\\\":{\\\"total\\\":0,\\\"todo\\\":0,\\\"active\\\":0,\\\"done\\\":0,\\\"closed\\\":0,\\\"blocked\\\":0},\\\"story\\\":{\\\"total\\\":0,\\\"todo\\\":0,\\\"active\\\":0,\\\"done\\\":0,\\\"closed\\\":0,\\\"blocked\\\":0},\\\"task\\\":{\\\"total\\\":1,\\\"todo\\\":0,\\\"active\\\":1,\\\"done\\\":0,\\\"closed\\\":0,\\\"blocked\\\":0}}}},\\\"outcomeResources\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1r9wrr_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260907-a6765b.log\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://TASK-260830-1r9wrr/TASK-260830-1r9wrr_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--muse-_RUN-260907-a6765b.log\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"System spawn log captured by task-board\\\"}],\\\"parent\\\":\\\"STORY-260830-3tq4ns\\\",\\\"preconditionResources\\\":[],\\\"review\\\":\\\"required\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); §2.3, §5.1-5.2, §5.7, §14.4. Work only inside the session-state-projection-and-name-resolution story boundary.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"task_class\\\":\\\"code\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-1r9wrr: implement-session-state-reducer\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"task\\\",\\\"updated\\\":\\\"2026-09-07T19:35:15Z\\\"}\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7086,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1772,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4b9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07d5e-0f16-71a3-abaf-54c2f5d26492"},"sequence":183,"recorded_at":1780531400000361,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf"},"call_id":"call_01a07d5e7a2a7950a20b8e6778e1c9b5","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree/internal/sessrepo/doc.go`.\n1|// Package sessrepo persists and validates AX Session Records and the\n2|// append-only per-session event chain with source sequence continuity.\n3|//\n4|// Normative scope: AX v0.5.0 sections 2.3 (session name resolution), 5.1\n5|// (Session Record), 5.2 (Session Event), 5.7 (derived session states), and\n6|// 14.4 (list and status fields). This package owns durable session state:\n7|// the immutable record, the ordered event chain beneath it, and the stored\n8|// identity fields that later leaves project into lifecycle state, resolved\n9|// names, and list/status rows.\n10|//\n11|// Division of authority inside this story:\n12|//\n13|//   - Validation of record and event closed shapes and of every self-identity\n14|//     digest is owned by internal/canonicaljson and reached only through its\n15|//     production VerifyObjectIdentity entry. Entry decodes refuse a foreign\n16|//     schema before Verify; the load path re-verifies stored blobs through\n17|//     Verify — recomputing whatever digest the bytes claim — and refuses a\n18|//     non-event_id self field or an index-disagreeing digest at its named\n19|//     arms. This package never re-decodes a frame, never recomputes a\n20|//     bound, and never selects a self field.\n21|//   - Strict frame decoding and scalar bound checks on the members this\n22|//     package must read (session and lease identifiers, lease_sequence,\n23|//     predecessor digests, names) are owned by internal/environ and\n24|//     internal/scalar and reached only through their production checks.\n25|//   - Crash-point vocabulary and outcomes are owned by\n26|//     internal/secconftest. The repository fires the owner's own points\n27|//     through the owner's Injector: a fault before the durable write carries\n28|//     safe_retry, a fault after it carries recoverable_parked_state, and a\n29|//     crashed commit counts as committed.\n30|//   - The refusal census denominator is derived from production through\n31|//     internal/invcore; see census_test.go.\n32|//\n33|// Per-session parked reporting (SPEC.md:9082, Section 13.13\n34|// recoverable_parked_state; Section 14.4 per-session warnings).\n35|//\n36|// ListSessions reports one entry per session directory in session-ID\n37|// order. A session whose bytes no longer verify is returned as a parked\n38|// entry — Parked=true with the blocking reason and the same-operation\n39|// retry — and never fails the listing for its healthy siblings. Resolve\n40|// routes only healthy sessions; a query naming only a parked session is\n41|// not found. GetRecord, GetEvent, and ListEvents still refuse a parked\n42|// session per session with the load failure.\n43|//\n44|// Why per-session instead of repository-wide closure: a repository-wide\n45|// listing error carries no per-session channel, so the Section 5.7\n46|// reducer and the Section 14.4 rendering leaves could not project the\n47|// parked lifecycle state, the blocking reason, or the warnings from what\n48|// this leaf exposes — and one torn session denied listing and name\n49|// resolution to every healthy sibling permanently when its original\n50|// bytes were lost. Per-session reporting keeps healthy sessions usable\n51|// while the parked session stays visible. The tradeoff is that callers\n52|// must check Parked: a listing that contains parked entries returns nil\n53|// error by design.\n54|//\n55|// Retry table (same-operation retry, Section 13.13):\n56|//\n57|//   - Bare session directory (no record.json, no chain.json): retry\n58|//     CreateSession with the session record for this session ID. Any\n59|//     valid record for the ID resumes; the parked state is the bare\n60|//     directory left by a crash between the directory and record steps.\n61|//   - Record parked without a chain index (record.json verifies, no\n62|//     chain.json): retry CreateSession with the byte-identical session\n63|//     record. A different record for the same session ID is refused\n64|//     with ErrSessionExists and the parked bytes survive; the\n65|//     byte-equality is full-content, not length-only.\n66|//   - Torn store (chain.json present but the session no longer\n67|//     verifies): no CreateSession retry heals it. A byte-identical\n68|//     retry is refused as an existing session and a differing retry is\n69|//     refused the same way; the store stays parked.\n70|//\n71|// Operator remedy. There is no delete, prune, or quarantine entry by\n72|// design: records and events are append-only and no production path\n73|// rewrites or deletes an existing entry. When no same-operation retry\n74|// heals a parked session — the original record bytes are lost, or the\n75|// store is torn past the create window — the operator removes the\n76|// session directory at <data-root>/sessions/<session-id> from the\n77|// filesystem after confirming no host will retry with the original\n78|// bytes, and the listing heals on the next read. Removing the directory\n79|// discards whatever that session had parked; it never touches siblings.\n80|// Downstream leaves consume the parked channel as: SessionSummary.Parked\n81|// selects the parked/failed lifecycle projection, BlockingReason feeds\n82|// status/doctor blocking reason and warnings, and RetryHint feeds the\n83|// retry or remedy line.\n84|//\n85|// Stated bounds (not silent gaps):\n86|//\n87|//   - Single authoritative branch. The repository tracks one ordered chain\n88|//     per session in arrival order. A same-epoch event under a different\n89|//     lease is preserved as an immutable blob but refused from the chain\n90|//     with ErrDivergentBranch; lease arbitration across partitions belongs\n91|//     to the ownership-leases story, not to this leaf.\n92|//   - No lifecycle derivation. Section 5.7 SessionState reduction and the\n93|//     full Section 2.3 four-step resolution order (peer-learned names,\n94|//     interactive choice) belong to the sibling reducer and name-resolution\n95|//     leaves. This package exposes the stored facts they project: exact\n96|//     local names with ASCII case-fold ambiguity detection, UUID routing,\n97|//     per-session chain heads, and the parked channel above.\n98|//   - No Section 14.4 rendering. ListSessions exposes stored identity plus\n99|//     chain-head facts (or the parked channel); human or JSON rendering\n100|//     of owner host, checkpoint age, capability status, and warnings\n101|//     belongs to the CLI surface leaf.\n102|//\n103|// The package adds no ax command, no doctor result, and no runtime\n104|// capability claim.\n105|package sessrepo","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
