{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c559","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07d5e-0f16-71a3-abaf-54c2f5d26492"},"sequence":263,"recorded_at":1780531400000521,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"9fb4ab12-b3e7-440d-97eb-9429839873f0"},"task_id":"9fb4ab12-b3e7-440d-97eb-9429839873f0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"9fb4ab12-b3e7-440d-97eb-9429839873f0","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(1937 line(s) above)\n1938|The winning lease is selected by the greatest tuple\n1939|<code>(epoch, lease_id)</code>, where <code>lease_id</code> uses bytewise UUID\n1940|order. Lease UUIDs are random UUIDv4 values, so wall-clock skew cannot bias the\n1941|tie-break. A valid epoch greater than 1 MUST name a known predecessor for the\n1942|same session, MUST equal that predecessor's epoch plus one, and MUST reference\n1943|a validated checkpoint for that session and predecessor lease. An epoch-1\n1944|<code>create</code> lease MUST have a null predecessor and MAY have a null\n1945|checkpoint before the first provider boundary exists. Every new takeover lease\n1946|MUST use <code>max_observed_epoch + 1</code> from the initiator's current union.\n1947|\n1948|The tuple rule handles concurrent force takeovers under partition without\n1949|clock ordering. Both processes can temporarily continue in isolated partitions,\n1950|which is why force takeover warns about split brain. After union, exactly one\n1951|lease wins. Events under the losing same-epoch lease and all lower epochs MUST\n1952|be preserved in a divergent branch and MUST NOT affect authoritative state.\n1953|\n1954|An owner process MUST revalidate its fencing token before:\n1955|\n1956|- accepting operator input after attach;\n1957|- starting a provider turn;\n1958|- publishing a checkpoint;\n1959|- pushing records or workspace changes; and\n1960|- resuming after any transport or sleep interruption longer than the configured\n1961|  lease refresh interval.\n1962|\n1963|There is no time-expiring ownership lease in v0.5.0. Liveness is not authority.\n1964|A host being offline does not make a replica owner; only a takeover or fork\n1965|does.\n1966|\n1967|### 5.4 Checkpoint Record\n1968|\n1969|The Checkpoint Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:checkpoint</code> version\n1970|<code>1.0.0</code>. Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n1971|\n1972|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1973|| --- | --- | --- |\n1974|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Checkpoint schema identifier |\n1975|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1976|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n1977|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1978|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing Session Record |\n1979|| <code>lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Greater than zero and equal to the referenced winning lease |\n1980|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Equal to that lease's fencing token |\n1981|| <code>safe_boundary</code> | Safe Boundary Evidence | Closed shape below |\n1982|| <code>event_heads</code> | sorted unique digest[1..64] | Authoritative event DAG heads immediately before this object |\n1983|| <code>workspace_manifest_id</code> | digest | Workspace-group Transfer Manifest root |\n1984|| <code>provider_manifest_id</code> | digest or null | Direct native-store/provider snapshot only |\n1985|| <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> | digest or null | Task-board path only |\n1986|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Current lease holder |\n1987|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n1988|| <code>status</code> | enum | Literal <code>validated</code> |\n1989|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1990|\n1991|Safe Boundary Evidence is a closed object containing exactly\n1992|<code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n1993|<code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>,\n1994|<code>evidence:provider_api|provider_event|managed_pty|task_board_bridge|accepted_test</code>,\n1995|<code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>,\n1996|<code>background_idle:boolean</code>, <code>open_processes:uint53</code>, and\n1997|<code>open_database_handles:uint53</code>. A published checkpoint requires all\n1998|three booleans true and both counters zero. Provider-specific scheduled or\n1999|child work is included in <code>background_idle</code> and\n2000|<code>open_processes</code>; an adapter that cannot prove it MUST NOT publish a\n2001|new checkpoint.\n2002|\n2003|The referenced Session Record selects the persistence variant. For\n2004|<code>kind = direct</code>, <code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be non-null\n2005|and <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be null. A backend-resolved provider\n2006|with no portable bytes still uses a provider Transfer Manifest containing its\n2007|validated identity and zero file entries; null is not used to erase that\n2008|distinction. For <code>kind = task_board</code>,\n2009|<code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be null and\n2010|<code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be non-null. Both-null and both-non-null\n2011|checkpoints are invalid.\n2012|\n2013|A checkpoint MUST NOT be published until every referenced object exists,\n2014|hashes correctly, passes schema validation, and the provider/task-board path\n2015|meets its quiescence requirement. A force takeover MAY select the newest\n2016|validated checkpoint even when no new safe checkpoint can be created.\n2017|\n2018|<code>event_heads</code> identifies the authoritative event DAG immediately\n2019|before the checkpoint object. A later <code>checkpoint.created</code> event MAY\n2020|reference that checkpoint and those heads; the checkpoint MUST NOT reference\n2021|the announcing event because that would create a circular digest dependency.\n2022|The transitive event-head closure also fixes the Section 2.4 effective\n2023|execution profile and its nullable source event for this checkpoint. A missing,\n2024|losing-lease, or non-newest <code>profile.changed</code> reference is\n2025|<code>integrity_failure</code>; checkpoint consumers MUST NOT consult a later\n2026|local-only profile event or fall back to the creation profile.\n2027|\n2028|Normative negative fixtures are: <code>CP-N1</code>, with\n2029|<code>background_idle = false</code> and status <code>validated</code>;\n2030|<code>CP-N2</code>, with a direct Session Record and null provider manifest;\n2031|<code>CP-N3</code>, with both persistence IDs non-null; and\n2032|<code>CP-N4</code>, with an unknown <code>safe_boundary.pid</code> member. Each\n2033|MUST be rejected with <code>incompatible_schema</code> before publication.\n2034|\n2035|Normative example:\n2036|\n2037|~~~json\n2038|{\n2039|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:checkpoint\",\n2040|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2041|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n2042|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2043|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2044|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n2045|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n2046|  \"safe_boundary\": {\n2047|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n2048|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n2049|    \"evidence\": \"accepted_test\",\n2050|    \"input_blocked\": true,\n2051|    \"foreground_idle\": true,\n2052|    \"background_idle\": true,\n2053|    \"open_processes\": 0,\n2054|    \"open_database_handles\": 0\n2055|  },\n2056|  \"event_heads\": [\n2057|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n2058|  ],\n2059|  \"workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n2060|  \"provider_manifest_id\": \"sha256:1e817955dcc529e282ab31f91c99561d03b3c5642282d2e0a0e05b0f60dd0f91\",\n2061|  \"task_board_bundle_id\": null,\n2062|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2063|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:30.000Z\",\n2064|  \"status\": \"validated\",\n2065|  \"extensions\": {}\n2066|}\n2067|~~~\n2068|\n2069|### 5.5 Provider Identity Record\n2070|\n2071|The Provider Identity Record schema is\n2072|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-identity</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its\n2073|top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n2074|\n2075|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n2076|| --- | --- | --- |\n2077|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Provider Identity schema identifier |\n2078|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n2079|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n2080|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n2081|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing logical session |\n2082|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id | Must equal the Session Record provider |\n2083|| <code>provider_version</code> | string[1..128] | Exact probed version |\n2084|| <code>provider_version_range</code> | string[1..256] | Adapter compatibility range used for this identity |\n2085|| <code>native_session_id</code> | string[1..512] | Opaque provider handle; never interpreted by core |\n2086|| <code>identity_kind</code> | enum | <code>session_uuid</code>, <code>session_path_or_id</code>, <code>backend_conversation_uuid</code>, <code>task_board_managed</code>, or <code>provider_defined</code> |\n2087|| <code>logical_workspace_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Member of the Session Record workspace group |\n2088|| <code>backend_realm_fingerprint</code> | digest or null | Non-secret fingerprint; non-null when backend/account realm is a resume precondition |\n2089|| <code>opaque_identity</code> | map(provider-identity-key,string[1..1024])[0..32] | Explicit adapter data map defined below |\n2090|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Identifying owner host |\n2091|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2092|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2093|\n2094|A provider-identity key matches <code>[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}</code>. Map keys\n2095|are data rather than schema members; values are non-secret strings only. This\n2096|is the sole provider-defined identity-data surface in version 1.0.0. It MUST\n2097|NOT contain an absolute path, credential, environment value, PID, socket,\n2098|terminal ID, or mutable cache selector. Structured or binary provider data\n2099|belongs in a content-addressed provider manifest, not this map.\n2100|\n2101|An absolute workspace path MAY appear only as source observation metadata. It\n2102|MUST NOT be part of the cross-host identity. The destination adapter MUST\n2103|derive native path keys from the destination workspace mapping.\n2104|\n2105|Normative negative fixtures are: unknown <code>identity_kind</code>; absent\n2106|<code>opaque_identity</code>; a map value that is an object instead of a\n2107|string; an absolute source path in that map; or an Antigravity\n2108|<code>backend_conversation_uuid</code> with null realm fingerprint. Each MUST\n2109|fail schema or provider-identity validation. A backend fingerprint is optional\n2110|for the other kinds unless that provider's Section 8 contract requires it.\n2111|\n2112|Normative example:\n2113|\n2114|~~~json\n2115|{\n2116|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n2117|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2118|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:c879d766da67a8cfb3a3f6eae2234faa5d52d8df987496eae2218f40e5e220c2\",\n2119|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2120|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2121|  \"provider_id\": \"antigravity\",\n2122|  \"provider_version\": \"1.1.14\",\n2123|  \"provider_version_range\": \">=1.1.14 <1.2.0\",\n2124|  \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n2125|  \"identity_kind\": \"backend_conversation_uuid\",\n2126|  \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n2127|  \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaad\",\n2128|  \"opaque_identity\": {},\n2129|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2130|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:45.000Z\",\n2131|  \"extensions\": {}\n2132|}\n2133|~~~\n2134|\n2135|### 5.6 Workspace Group Record\n2136|\n2137|The Workspace Group Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:workspace-group</code>\n2138|version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its closed top-level shape contains exactly\n2139|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n2140|<code>record_id:digest</code>, <code>subject_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n2141|<code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n2142|<code>display_name:string[1..128]</code>,\n2143|<code>members:WorkspaceMember[1..256]</code>,\n2144|<code>created_by_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>created_at:timestamp</code>, and\n2145|<code>extensions:object</code>. Subject and workspace-group IDs MUST be equal.\n2146|Members are sorted by <code>workspace_id</code>, and no two members may have an\n2147|equal or case-colliding <code>group_relative_path</code>.\n2148|\n2149|The record defines immutable workspace topology, not evolving session\n2150|membership. Exactly one schema-valid Workspace Group Record may exist for a\n2151|<code>workspace_group_id</code>. Two different record IDs with that same group\n2152|ID are <code>integrity_failure</code>; the group and every referring session\n2153|MUST park until the conflicting history is reconciled. Changing the workspace\n2154|member set or its logical identities requires a new workspace group and new or\n2155|forked Session Records; no group-update winner is inferred from timestamps.\n2156|\n2157|<code>WorkspaceMember</code> is a closed tagged union. No member-level\n2158|<code>extensions</code> map exists in 1.0.0; unknown members are rejected:\n2159|\n2160|| Tag | Exact members |\n2161|| --- | --- |\n2162|| <code>kind = git</code> | <code>workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>kind:git</code>, <code>group_relative_path:path</code>, <code>repository_identity:string[1..256]</code>, <code>sanitized_remote_urls:sorted unique sanitized-git-URL[1..16]</code>, <code>repo_relative_cwd:.&#124;path</code>, <code>agent_project_config_paths:sorted unique path[0..256]</code>, <code>materialization_policy:shared_checkout&#124;separate_worktree</code> |\n2163|| <code>kind = managed_tree</code> | <code>workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>kind:managed_tree</code>, <code>group_relative_path:path</code>, <code>tree_identity:string[1..256]</code>, <code>repo_relative_cwd:.&#124;path</code>, <code>agent_project_config_paths:sorted unique path[0..256]</code>, <code>materialization_policy:shared_tree&#124;separate_copy</code> |\n2164|\n2165|A sanitized Git URL uses <code>https</code>, <code>ssh</code>, or provider-neutral\n2166|<code>git</code> syntax and MUST contain no password, token, query, fragment, or\n2167|machine-local file path. <code>repository_identity</code> and\n2168|<code>tree_identity</code> are logical labels, not absolute paths. Every cwd and\n2169|project-config path is relative to that member and MUST exist in the referenced\n2170|workspace snapshot when materialized.\n2171|\n2172|If multiple active sessions share a checkout or managed tree, takeover MUST migrate the whole\n2173|workspace group or materialize separate worktrees. It MUST NOT move one session\n2174|onto a concurrently mutated shared directory.\n2175|\n2176|Normative example:\n2177|\n2178|~~~json\n2179|{\n2180|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:workspace-group\",\n2181|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2182|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:3b366ca989681c63323c5de6db28198796aa913947ad3cd9456fc6dcee62b743\",\n2183|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n2184|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n2185|  \"display_name\": \"payments\",\n2186|  \"members\": [\n2187|    {\n2188|      \"workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n2189|      \"kind\": \"git\",\n2190|      \"group_relative_path\": \"payments-api\",\n2191|      \"repository_identity\": \"relux/payments-api\",\n2192|      \"sanitized_remote_urls\": [\"ssh://git@github.com/relux/payments-api.git\"],\n2193|      \"repo_relative_cwd\": \"src\",\n2194|      \"agent_project_config_paths\": [\"AGENTS.md\"],\n2195|      \"materialization_policy\": \"separate_worktree\"\n2196|    },\n2197|    {\n2198|      \"workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\n2199|      \"kind\": \"managed_tree\",\n2200|      \"group_relative_path\": \"design-notes\",\n2201|      \"tree_identity\": \"relux/design-notes\",\n2202|      \"repo_relative_cwd\": \"drafts\",\n2203|      \"agent_project_config_paths\": [\"AGENTS.md\"],\n2204|      \"materialization_policy\": \"separate_copy\"\n2205|    }\n2206|  ],\n2207|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2208|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:50.000Z\",\n2209|  \"extensions\": {}\n2210|}\n2211|~~~\n2212|\n2213|The managed-tree member above is also a standalone positive tagged-union\n2214|fixture:\n2215|\n2216|~~~json\n2217|{\n2218|  \"workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\n2219|  \"kind\": \"managed_tree\",\n2220|  \"group_relative_path\": \"design-notes\",\n2221|  \"tree_identity\": \"relux/design-notes\",\n2222|  \"repo_relative_cwd\": \"drafts\",\n2223|  \"agent_project_config_paths\": [\"AGENTS.md\"],\n2224|  \"materialization_policy\": \"separate_copy\"\n2225|}\n2226|~~~\n2227|\n2228|<code>WG-N1</code> adds <code>sanitized_remote_urls</code> to that\n2229|managed-tree variant, <code>WG-N2</code> omits <code>repository_identity</code>\n2230|from the Git variant, <code>WG-N3</code> uses\n2231|<code>separate_worktree</code> on a managed tree, and <code>WG-N4</code> adds an\n2232|unknown nested member. All four fixtures MUST be rejected.\n2233|\n2234|Session membership is derived, never selected from competing group records.\n2235|For a converged immutable-object set, <code>all_members(G)</code> is the\n2236|bytewise-sorted set of Session Records whose <code>workspace_group_id = G</code>.\n2237|<code>live_members(G)</code> removes only sessions with an authoritative\n2238|Section 10.7 session Tombstone. Stop does not remove membership, and a Session\n2239|Record can never move to another group. A logical leave therefore means an\n2240|authorized session Tombstone; continuing work in another topology means a new\n2241|or forked Session Record.\n2242|\n2243|The active shared-checkout set for a host H is the subset of\n2244|<code>live_members(G)</code> whose winning lifecycle is <code>running</code>,\n2245|<code>idle</code>, <code>quiescing</code>, or <code>checkpointing</code> and whose\n2246|local managed-replica marker names the same shared checkout/tree on H. A\n2247|takeover MaterializationCohort MUST include that complete set and MAY also\n2248|include stopped selected members; a stopped-only owner therefore has a valid\n2249|one-member cohort. Passive sync and owner resume instead use an empty ownership-\n2250|transfer set as Section 11.3 requires. The complete live-member records form\n2251|the WorkspaceGroupExpectation; the separately typed MaterializationCohort\n2252|selects materialization and ownership transfer. Every prepare, stop, lease,\n2253|materialization, and resume phase MUST revalidate both applicable objects. A\n2254|concurrent join or authoritative leave invalidates the expectation and fails\n2255|the group operation with <code>workspace_group_changed</code> before another\n2256|member is activated.\n2257|\n2258|Normative convergence fixtures are:\n2259|\n2260|| Fixture | Union input | Required result |\n2261|| --- | --- | --- |\n2262|| <code>WG-JOIN-CONCURRENT</code> | Two valid new Session Records independently reference G | Both record IDs appear in <code>all_members(G)</code>; no record wins or is discarded |\n2263|| <code>WG-LEAVE-CONCURRENT</code> | A valid new Session Record and an authoritative session Tombstone for a different member arrive in either order | The join is present and the tombstoned member is absent from <code>live_members(G)</code>; order does not matter |\n2264|| <code>WG-MOVE-N1</code> | An implementation attempts to rewrite an existing Session Record to another group | Reject the different bytes/identity; require a new session or fork |\n2265|| <code>WG-GROUP-CONFLICT-N1</code> | Two distinct Workspace Group Records claim G | <code>integrity_failure</code>; park all referring sessions; no timestamp winner |\n2266|| <code>WG-TAKEOVER-CONCURRENT-N1</code> | Membership changes after group prepare | Abort before activation, retain staging, recompute the expectation, and retry |\n2267|\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07d5e-0f16-71a3-abaf-54c2f5d26492"},"sequence":264,"recorded_at":1780531400000523,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"9fb4ab12-b3e7-440d-97eb-9429839873f0"},"task_id":"9fb4ab12-b3e7-440d-97eb-9429839873f0","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"9fb4ab12-b3e7-440d-97eb-9429839873f0"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07d5e-0f16-71a3-abaf-54c2f5d26492"},"sequence":265,"recorded_at":1780531400000525,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf"},"call_id":"call_01a07d5ea65c71b0b587131ebc781feb","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(1937 line(s) above)\n1938|The winning lease is selected by the greatest tuple\n1939|<code>(epoch, lease_id)</code>, where <code>lease_id</code> uses bytewise UUID\n1940|order. Lease UUIDs are random UUIDv4 values, so wall-clock skew cannot bias the\n1941|tie-break. A valid epoch greater than 1 MUST name a known predecessor for the\n1942|same session, MUST equal that predecessor's epoch plus one, and MUST reference\n1943|a validated checkpoint for that session and predecessor lease. An epoch-1\n1944|<code>create</code> lease MUST have a null predecessor and MAY have a null\n1945|checkpoint before the first provider boundary exists. Every new takeover lease\n1946|MUST use <code>max_observed_epoch + 1</code> from the initiator's current union.\n1947|\n1948|The tuple rule handles concurrent force takeovers under partition without\n1949|clock ordering. Both processes can temporarily continue in isolated partitions,\n1950|which is why force takeover warns about split brain. After union, exactly one\n1951|lease wins. Events under the losing same-epoch lease and all lower epochs MUST\n1952|be preserved in a divergent branch and MUST NOT affect authoritative state.\n1953|\n1954|An owner process MUST revalidate its fencing token before:\n1955|\n1956|- accepting operator input after attach;\n1957|- starting a provider turn;\n1958|- publishing a checkpoint;\n1959|- pushing records or workspace changes; and\n1960|- resuming after any transport or sleep interruption longer than the configured\n1961|  lease refresh interval.\n1962|\n1963|There is no time-expiring ownership lease in v0.5.0. Liveness is not authority.\n1964|A host being offline does not make a replica owner; only a takeover or fork\n1965|does.\n1966|\n1967|### 5.4 Checkpoint Record\n1968|\n1969|The Checkpoint Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:checkpoint</code> version\n1970|<code>1.0.0</code>. Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n1971|\n1972|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1973|| --- | --- | --- |\n1974|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Checkpoint schema identifier |\n1975|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1976|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n1977|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1978|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing Session Record |\n1979|| <code>lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Greater than zero and equal to the referenced winning lease |\n1980|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Equal to that lease's fencing token |\n1981|| <code>safe_boundary</code> | Safe Boundary Evidence | Closed shape below |\n1982|| <code>event_heads</code> | sorted unique digest[1..64] | Authoritative event DAG heads immediately before this object |\n1983|| <code>workspace_manifest_id</code> | digest | Workspace-group Transfer Manifest root |\n1984|| <code>provider_manifest_id</code> | digest or null | Direct native-store/provider snapshot only |\n1985|| <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> | digest or null | Task-board path only |\n1986|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Current lease holder |\n1987|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n1988|| <code>status</code> | enum | Literal <code>validated</code> |\n1989|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n1990|\n1991|Safe Boundary Evidence is a closed object containing exactly\n1992|<code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n1993|<code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>,\n1994|<code>evidence:provider_api|provider_event|managed_pty|task_board_bridge|accepted_test</code>,\n1995|<code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>,\n1996|<code>background_idle:boolean</code>, <code>open_processes:uint53</code>, and\n1997|<code>open_database_handles:uint53</code>. A published checkpoint requires all\n1998|three booleans true and both counters zero. Provider-specific scheduled or\n1999|child work is included in <code>background_idle</code> and\n2000|<code>open_processes</code>; an adapter that cannot prove it MUST NOT publish a\n2001|new checkpoint.\n2002|\n2003|The referenced Session Record selects the persistence variant. For\n2004|<code>kind = direct</code>, <code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be non-null\n2005|and <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be null. A backend-resolved provider\n2006|with no portable bytes still uses a provider Transfer Manifest containing its\n2007|validated identity and zero file entries; null is not used to erase that\n2008|distinction. For <code>kind = task_board</code>,\n2009|<code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be null and\n2010|<code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be non-null. Both-null and both-non-null\n2011|checkpoints are invalid.\n2012|\n2013|A checkpoint MUST NOT be published until every referenced object exists,\n2014|hashes correctly, passes schema validation, and the provider/task-board path\n2015|meets its quiescence requirement. A force takeover MAY select the newest\n2016|validated checkpoint even when no new safe checkpoint can be created.\n2017|\n2018|<code>event_heads</code> identifies the authoritative event DAG immediately\n2019|before the checkpoint object. A later <code>checkpoint.created</code> event MAY\n2020|reference that checkpoint and those heads; the checkpoint MUST NOT reference\n2021|the announcing event because that would create a circular digest dependency.\n2022|The transitive event-head closure also fixes the Section 2.4 effective\n2023|execution profile and its nullable source event for this checkpoint. A missing,\n2024|losing-lease, or non-newest <code>profile.changed</code> reference is\n2025|<code>integrity_failure</code>; checkpoint consumers MUST NOT consult a later\n2026|local-only profile event or fall back to the creation profile.\n2027|\n2028|Normative negative fixtures are: <code>CP-N1</code>, with\n2029|<code>background_idle = false</code> and status <code>validated</code>;\n2030|<code>CP-N2</code>, with a direct Session Record and null provider manifest;\n2031|<code>CP-N3</code>, with both persistence IDs non-null; and\n2032|<code>CP-N4</code>, with an unknown <code>safe_boundary.pid</code> member. Each\n2033|MUST be rejected with <code>incompatible_schema</code> before publication.\n2034|\n2035|Normative example:\n2036|\n2037|~~~json\n2038|{\n2039|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:checkpoint\",\n2040|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2041|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n2042|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2043|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2044|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n2045|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n2046|  \"safe_boundary\": {\n2047|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n2048|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n2049|    \"evidence\": \"accepted_test\",\n2050|    \"input_blocked\": true,\n2051|    \"foreground_idle\": true,\n2052|    \"background_idle\": true,\n2053|    \"open_processes\": 0,\n2054|    \"open_database_handles\": 0\n2055|  },\n2056|  \"event_heads\": [\n2057|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n2058|  ],\n2059|  \"workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n2060|  \"provider_manifest_id\": \"sha256:1e817955dcc529e282ab31f91c99561d03b3c5642282d2e0a0e05b0f60dd0f91\",\n2061|  \"task_board_bundle_id\": null,\n2062|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2063|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:30.000Z\",\n2064|  \"status\": \"validated\",\n2065|  \"extensions\": {}\n2066|}\n2067|~~~\n2068|\n2069|### 5.5 Provider Identity Record\n2070|\n2071|The Provider Identity Record schema is\n2072|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-identity</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its\n2073|top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n2074|\n2075|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n2076|| --- | --- | --- |\n2077|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Provider Identity schema identifier |\n2078|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n2079|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n2080|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n2081|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing logical session |\n2082|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id | Must equal the Session Record provider |\n2083|| <code>provider_version</code> | string[1..128] | Exact probed version |\n2084|| <code>provider_version_range</code> | string[1..256] | Adapter compatibility range used for this identity |\n2085|| <code>native_session_id</code> | string[1..512] | Opaque provider handle; never interpreted by core |\n2086|| <code>identity_kind</code> | enum | <code>session_uuid</code>, <code>session_path_or_id</code>, <code>backend_conversation_uuid</code>, <code>task_board_managed</code>, or <code>provider_defined</code> |\n2087|| <code>logical_workspace_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Member of the Session Record workspace group |\n2088|| <code>backend_realm_fingerprint</code> | digest or null | Non-secret fingerprint; non-null when backend/account realm is a resume precondition |\n2089|| <code>opaque_identity</code> | map(provider-identity-key,string[1..1024])[0..32] | Explicit adapter data map defined below |\n2090|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Identifying owner host |\n2091|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2092|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2093|\n2094|A provider-identity key matches <code>[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}</code>. Map keys\n2095|are data rather than schema members; values are non-secret strings only. This\n2096|is the sole provider-defined identity-data surface in version 1.0.0. It MUST\n2097|NOT contain an absolute path, credential, environment value, PID, socket,\n2098|terminal ID, or mutable cache selector. Structured or binary provider data\n2099|belongs in a content-addressed provider manifest, not this map.\n2100|\n2101|An absolute workspace path MAY appear only as source observation metadata. It\n2102|MUST NOT be part of the cross-host identity. The destination adapter MUST\n2103|derive native path keys from the destination workspace mapping.\n2104|\n2105|Normative negative fixtures are: unknown <code>identity_kind</code>; absent\n2106|<code>opaque_identity</code>; a map value that is an object instead of a\n2107|string; an absolute source path in that map; or an Antigravity\n2108|<code>backend_conversation_uuid</code> with null realm fingerprint. Each MUST\n2109|fail schema or provider-identity validation. A backend fingerprint is optional\n2110|for the other kinds unless that provider's Section 8 contract requires it.\n2111|\n2112|Normative example:\n2113|\n2114|~~~json\n2115|{\n2116|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n2117|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2118|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:c879d766da67a8cfb3a3f6eae2234faa5d52d8df987496eae2218f40e5e220c2\",\n2119|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2120|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2121|  \"provider_id\": \"antigravity\",\n2122|  \"provider_version\": \"1.1.14\",\n2123|  \"provider_version_range\": \">=1.1.14 <1.2.0\",\n2124|  \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n2125|  \"identity_kind\": \"backend_conversation_uuid\",\n2126|  \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n2127|  \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaad\",\n2128|  \"opaque_identity\": {},\n2129|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2130|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:45.000Z\",\n2131|  \"extensions\": {}\n2132|}\n2133|~~~\n2134|\n2135|### 5.6 Workspace Group Record\n2136|\n2137|The Workspace Group Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:workspace-group</code>\n2138|version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its closed top-level shape contains exactly\n2139|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n2140|<code>record_id:digest</code>, <code>subject_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n2141|<code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n2142|<code>display_name:string[1..128]</code>,\n2143|<code>members:WorkspaceMember[1..256]</code>,\n2144|<code>created_by_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>created_at:timestamp</code>, and\n2145|<code>extensions:object</code>. Subject and workspace-group IDs MUST be equal.\n2146|Members are sorted by <code>workspace_id</code>, and no two members may have an\n2147|equal or case-colliding <code>group_relative_path</code>.\n2148|\n2149|The record defines immutable workspace topology, not evolving session\n2150|membership. Exactly one schema-valid Workspace Group Record may exist for a\n2151|<code>workspace_group_id</code>. Two different record IDs with that same group\n2152|ID are <code>integrity_failure</code>; the group and every referring session\n2153|MUST park until the conflicting history is reconciled. Changing the workspace\n2154|member set or its logical identities requires a new workspace group and new or\n2155|forked Session Records; no group-update winner is inferred from timestamps.\n2156|\n2157|<code>WorkspaceMember</code> is a closed tagged union. No member-level\n2158|<code>extensions</code> map exists in 1.0.0; unknown members are rejected:\n2159|\n2160|| Tag | Exact members |\n2161|| --- | --- |\n2162|| <code>kind = git</code> | <code>workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>kind:git</code>, <code>group_relative_path:path</code>, <code>repository_identity:string[1..256]</code>, <code>sanitized_remote_urls:sorted unique sanitized-git-URL[1..16]</code>, <code>repo_relative_cwd:.&#124;path</code>, <code>agent_project_config_paths:sorted unique path[0..256]</code>, <code>materialization_policy:shared_checkout&#124;separate_worktree</code> |\n2163|| <code>kind = managed_tree</code> | <code>workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>kind:managed_tree</code>, <code>group_relative_path:path</code>, <code>tree_identity:string[1..256]</code>, <code>repo_relative_cwd:.&#124;path</code>, <code>agent_project_config_paths:sorted unique path[0..256]</code>, <code>materialization_policy:shared_tree&#124;separate_copy</code> |\n2164|\n2165|A sanitized Git URL uses <code>https</code>, <code>ssh</code>, or provider-neutral\n2166|<code>git</code> syntax and MUST contain no password, token, query, fragment, or\n2167|machine-local file path. <code>repository_identity</code> and\n2168|<code>tree_identity</code> are logical labels, not absolute paths. Every cwd and\n2169|project-config path is relative to that member and MUST exist in the referenced\n2170|workspace snapshot when materialized.\n2171|\n2172|If multiple active sessions share a checkout or managed tree, takeover MUST migrate the whole\n2173|workspace group or materialize separate worktrees. It MUST NOT move one session\n2174|onto a concurrently mutated shared directory.\n2175|\n2176|Normative example:\n2177|\n2178|~~~json\n2179|{\n2180|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:workspace-group\",\n2181|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2182|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:3b366ca989681c63323c5de6db28198796aa913947ad3cd9456fc6dcee62b743\",\n2183|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n2184|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n2185|  \"display_name\": \"payments\",\n2186|  \"members\": [\n2187|    {\n2188|      \"workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n2189|      \"kind\": \"git\",\n2190|      \"group_relative_path\": \"payments-api\",\n2191|      \"repository_identity\": \"relux/payments-api\",\n2192|      \"sanitized_remote_urls\": [\"ssh://git@github.com/relux/payments-api.git\"],\n2193|      \"repo_relative_cwd\": \"src\",\n2194|      \"agent_project_config_paths\": [\"AGENTS.md\"],\n2195|      \"materialization_policy\": \"separate_worktree\"\n2196|    },\n2197|    {\n2198|      \"workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\n2199|      \"kind\": \"managed_tree\",\n2200|      \"group_relative_path\": \"design-notes\",\n2201|      \"tree_identity\": \"relux/design-notes\",\n2202|      \"repo_relative_cwd\": \"drafts\",\n2203|      \"agent_project_config_paths\": [\"AGENTS.md\"],\n2204|      \"materialization_policy\": \"separate_copy\"\n2205|    }\n2206|  ],\n2207|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2208|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:50.000Z\",\n2209|  \"extensions\": {}\n2210|}\n2211|~~~\n2212|\n2213|The managed-tree member above is also a standalone positive tagged-union\n2214|fixture:\n2215|\n2216|~~~json\n2217|{\n2218|  \"workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-2234567890ab\",\n2219|  \"kind\": \"managed_tree\",\n2220|  \"group_relative_path\": \"design-notes\",\n2221|  \"tree_identity\": \"relux/design-notes\",\n2222|  \"repo_relative_cwd\": \"drafts\",\n2223|  \"agent_project_config_paths\": [\"AGENTS.md\"],\n2224|  \"materialization_policy\": \"separate_copy\"\n2225|}\n2226|~~~\n2227|\n2228|<code>WG-N1</code> adds <code>sanitized_remote_urls</code> to that\n2229|managed-tree variant, <code>WG-N2</code> omits <code>repository_identity</code>\n2230|from the Git variant, <code>WG-N3</code> uses\n2231|<code>separate_worktree</code> on a managed tree, and <code>WG-N4</code> adds an\n2232|unknown nested member. All four fixtures MUST be rejected.\n2233|\n2234|Session membership is derived, never selected from competing group records.\n2235|For a converged immutable-object set, <code>all_members(G)</code> is the\n2236|bytewise-sorted set of Session Records whose <code>workspace_group_id = G</code>.\n2237|<code>live_members(G)</code> removes only sessions with an authoritative\n2238|Section 10.7 session Tombstone. Stop does not remove membership, and a Session\n2239|Record can never move to another group. A logical leave therefore means an\n2240|authorized session Tombstone; continuing work in another topology means a new\n2241|or forked Session Record.\n2242|\n2243|The active shared-checkout set for a host H is the subset of\n2244|<code>live_members(G)</code> whose winning lifecycle is <code>running</code>,\n2245|<code>idle</code>, <code>quiescing</code>, or <code>checkpointing</code> and whose\n2246|local managed-replica marker names the same shared checkout/tree on H. A\n2247|takeover MaterializationCohort MUST include that complete set and MAY also\n2248|include stopped selected members; a stopped-only owner therefore has a valid\n2249|one-member cohort. Passive sync and owner resume instead use an empty ownership-\n2250|transfer set as Section 11.3 requires. The complete live-member records form\n2251|the WorkspaceGroupExpectation; the separately typed MaterializationCohort\n2252|selects materialization and ownership transfer. Every prepare, stop, lease,\n2253|materialization, and resume phase MUST revalidate both applicable objects. A\n2254|concurrent join or authoritative leave invalidates the expectation and fails\n2255|the group operation with <code>workspace_group_changed</code> before another\n2256|member is activated.\n2257|\n2258|Normative convergence fixtures are:\n2259|\n2260|| Fixture | Union input | Required result |\n2261|| --- | --- | --- |\n2262|| <code>WG-JOIN-CONCURRENT</code> | Two valid new Session Records independently reference G | Both record IDs appear in <code>all_members(G)</code>; no record wins or is discarded |\n2263|| <code>WG-LEAVE-CONCURRENT</code> | A valid new Session Record and an authoritative session Tombstone for a different member arrive in either order | The join is present and the tombstoned member is absent from <code>live_members(G)</code>; order does not matter |\n2264|| <code>WG-MOVE-N1</code> | An implementation attempts to rewrite an existing Session Record to another group | Reject the different bytes/identity; require a new session or fork |\n2265|| <code>WG-GROUP-CONFLICT-N1</code> | Two distinct Workspace Group Records claim G | <code>integrity_failure</code>; park all referring sessions; no timestamp winner |\n2266|| <code>WG-TAKEOVER-CONCURRENT-N1</code> | Membership changes after group prepare | Abort before activation, retain staging, recompute the expectation, and retry |\n2267|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
