{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c57d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07d5e-0f16-71a3-abaf-54c2f5d26492"},"sequence":281,"recorded_at":1780531400000557,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"856dbc62-e8b6-4fad-b436-ef1ae6eda625"},"task_id":"856dbc62-e8b6-4fad-b436-ef1ae6eda625","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"856dbc62-e8b6-4fad-b436-ef1ae6eda625","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(2267 line(s) above)\n2268|### 5.7 Derived session states\n2269|\n2270|The state engine derives exactly one state for each\n2271|<code>(session_id, host_id)</code> projection and separately reports the\n2272|winning owner's projection as the session lifecycle state. Thus a destination\n2273|can be <code>running</code> while an old host is locally <code>stale</code>:\n2274|\n2275|| State | Meaning |\n2276|| --- | --- |\n2277|| <code>creating</code> | Session record and initial lease exist; no first validated checkpoint exists and bootstrap launch/retry is in progress |\n2278|| <code>running</code> | Winning owner has a live provider turn or accepts input |\n2279|| <code>idle</code> | Owner is live at an adapter-proven safe turn boundary |\n2280|| <code>quiescing</code> | New input is blocked while waiting for a safe boundary and clean stop |\n2281|| <code>checkpointing</code> | Safe state is being captured and validated |\n2282|| <code>stopped</code> | Winning owner has no provider process and a non-null validated checkpoint from which it is resumable |\n2283|| <code>materializing</code> | Destination staging/validation is in progress; it is not owner-active |\n2284|| <code>parked</code> | Wrapper exists but refuses provider launch due to remote/unknown ownership |\n2285|| <code>failed</code> | An operation failed and recovery metadata exists |\n2286|| <code>stale</code> | Local process/replica has a losing fencing token |\n2287|| <code>tombstoned</code> | Session is logically deleted and cannot resume |\n2288|\n2289|The exact <code>SessionState</code> enum is, in this order,\n2290|<code>creating</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>idle</code>,\n2291|<code>quiescing</code>, <code>checkpointing</code>, <code>stopped</code>,\n2292|<code>materializing</code>, <code>parked</code>, <code>failed</code>,\n2293|<code>stale</code>, and <code>tombstoned</code>. Every RPC and CLI field typed\n2294|<code>SessionState</code> uses exactly this registry. The spellings\n2295|<code>created</code>, <code>starting</code>, and <code>quiesced</code> are not\n2296|session lifecycle states in Session Record 1.0.0; a subsystem-specific bridge state\n2297|MAY use <code>quiesced</code> only where Section 9 declares that separate enum.\n2298|\n2299|Allowed transitions are:\n2300|\n2301|~~~text\n2302|creating -> running | idle | failed\n2303|running -> idle | quiescing | failed | stale\n2304|idle -> running | quiescing | checkpointing | stopped | stale\n2305|quiescing -> idle | checkpointing | failed | stale\n2306|checkpointing -> idle | stopped | materializing | failed\n2307|materializing -> stopped | running | parked | failed\n2308|stopped -> materializing | running | parked | tombstoned\n2309|parked -> materializing | running | stopped | stale\n2310|failed -> creating | stopped | parked | materializing | stale | tombstoned\n2311|stale -> stopped | tombstoned\n2312|~~~\n2313|\n2314|Any transition not listed MUST fail with <code>invalid_state_transition</code>.\n2315|Force takeover changes the old host's derived state to <code>stale</code> after\n2316|lease convergence even if its process remains alive.\n2317|\n2318|The <code>failed -> creating</code> edge is permitted only for an epoch-1\n2319|session with no validated checkpoint, the same winning create lease, no\n2320|authoritative <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event, and the Section 13.1\n2321|bootstrap-retry preconditions. A force-closed bootstrap remains\n2322|<code>failed</code> and non-resumable. No event or RPC result may derive\n2323|<code>stopped</code> while <code>newest_checkpoint_id</code> is null.\n2324|\n2325|## 6. Configuration contract\n2326|\n2327|### 6.1 Loading and precedence\n2328|\n2329|Configuration schema <code>urn:ax:schema:config</code> version\n2330|<code>1.0.0</code> is encoded as TOML. Precedence, highest first, is:\n2331|\n2332|1. command flags;\n2333|2. the five documented Section 3.2 <code>AX_*</code> path overrides;\n2334|3. values in the selected configuration file; and\n2335|4. normative defaults in this section.\n2336|\n2337|The configuration file itself is selected by <code>--config</code>, then\n2338|<code>AX_CONFIG</code>, then the platform-default configuration directory's\n2339|<code>config.toml</code>. The data, state, cache, and runtime overrides select\n2340|infrastructure roots and are not TOML field-by-field overrides. The same\n2341|resolved roots MUST be used by the CLI, service, RPC server, provider host, and\n2342|crash recovery for the entire process lifetime.\n2343|\n2344|Unknown top-level keys MUST fail configuration loading. Secret values MUST NOT\n2345|be accepted in config fields; a provider MAY name a machine-local environment\n2346|variable or credential profile.\n2347|\n2348|The complete 1.0.0 environment-override registry is\n2349|<code>AX_CONFIG</code>, <code>AX_DATA_DIR</code>,\n2350|<code>AX_STATE_DIR</code>, <code>AX_CACHE_DIR</code>, and\n2351|<code>AX_RUNTIME_DIR</code>, with the value kinds and empty-value rule in\n2352|Section 3.2. There are no other field-by-field <code>AX_*</code> overrides in\n2353|this version. Provider credential variables are destination-local inputs and\n2354|never configuration values.\n2355|\n2356|### 6.2 Normative example\n2357|\n2358|~~~toml\n2359|schema = \"urn:ax:schema:config\"\n2360|schema_version = \"1.0.0\"\n2361|host_id = \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\"\n2362|host_name = \"mbp-ivan\"\n2363|platform = \"macos\"\n2364|\n2365|[mesh]\n2366|transport = \"ssh\"\n2367|sync_interval_seconds = 60\n2368|connect_timeout_seconds = 10\n2369|rpc_timeout_seconds = 300\n2370|workspace_replication = true\n2371|payload_encryption = \"none\"\n2372|\n2373|[[mesh.peers]]\n2374|host_id = \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\"\n2375|name = \"workstation\"\n2376|endpoint = \"ivan@workstation.tailnet.ts.net\"\n2377|platform = \"linux\"\n2378|ssh_args = [\"-o\", \"BatchMode=yes\"]\n2379|\n2380|[[mesh.peers.workspace_roots]]\n2381|logical_root = \"relux\"\n2382|path = \"/srv/relux\"\n2383|\n2384|[[workspace_roots]]\n2385|logical_root = \"relux\"\n2386|path = \"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks\"\n2387|\n2388|[providers]\n2389|plugin_dirs = [\"/Users/iv/.local/libexec/ax/providers\"]\n2390|allow_path_plugins = true\n2391|require_explicit_trust = true\n2392|\n2393|[sync]\n2394|chunk_bytes = 4194304\n2395|max_parallel_chunks = 4\n2396|staging_retention_hours = 72\n2397|tombstone_min_retention_days = 90\n2398|\n2399|[terminal]\n2400|backend = \"tmux\"\n2401|safe_boundary_timeout_seconds = 300\n2402|graceful_stop_timeout_seconds = 60\n2403|\n2404|[service]\n2405|enabled = true\n2406|health_interval_seconds = 30\n2407|\n2408|[restore]\n2409|auto_resume = false\n2410|\n2411|[profiles.yolo]\n2412|require_first_use_confirmation = true\n2413|~~~\n2414|\n2415|On native Windows, a workspace mapping is written with a quoted TOML string\n2416|such as <code>path = \"D:\\\\Developer\\\\ReluxWorks\"</code>, and terminal backend\n2417|MUST be <code>conpty</code>. WSL2 configuration uses Linux paths and\n2418|<code>platform = \"wsl2\"</code>.\n2419|\n2420|### 6.3 Field constraints\n2421|\n2422|<code>platform</code> is one of <code>macos</code>, <code>linux</code>,\n2423|<code>wsl2</code>, or <code>windows</code>. A peer is authorized only when its\n2424|stable <code>host_id</code> appears in <code>mesh.peers</code> and the SSH\n2425|endpoint resolves to the authenticated host expected by SSH host-key policy.\n2426|Tailscale discovery MAY suggest a candidate configuration but MUST NOT write or\n2427|authorize it automatically.\n2428|\n2429|<code>mesh.payload_encryption</code> MUST be <code>none</code> in v0.3.0.\n2430|Other values MUST fail as unsupported. SSH supplies transport protection; this\n2431|setting prevents a misleading at-rest encryption claim.\n2432|\n2433|<code>sync.chunk_bytes</code> MUST equal 4,194,304 in Configuration 1.0.0.\n2434|Implementations MAY expose the field for forward compatibility but MUST reject\n2435|another value in this protocol version.\n2436|\n2437|Workspace roots MUST have unique <code>logical_root</code> values. Paths MAY\n2438|differ across hosts. A materializer MUST map a workspace using\n2439|<code>logical_root</code> plus a validated relative path, never a source\n2440|absolute path.\n2441|\n2442|The complete v1 field/default contract is:\n2443|\n2444|| Key | Required/default | Constraint |\n2445|| --- | --- | --- |\n2446|| <code>schema</code> | Required | Exact config schema identifier |\n2447|| <code>schema_version</code> | Required | Compatible version negotiated by this binary |\n2448|| <code>host_id</code> | Required | Stable UUIDv7; changing it creates a new mesh host |\n2449|| <code>host_name</code> | Required | 1–64 printable non-control UTF-8 characters |\n2450|| <code>platform</code> | Required | One of the four values above; MUST match runtime probe |\n2451|| <code>mesh.transport</code> | Default <code>ssh</code> | Only <code>ssh</code> in v0.3.0 |\n2452|| <code>mesh.sync_interval_seconds</code> | Default 60 | Integer 5–86,400 |\n2453|| <code>mesh.connect_timeout_seconds</code> | Default 10 | Integer 1–300 |\n2454|| <code>mesh.rpc_timeout_seconds</code> | Default 300 | Integer 10–3,600 |\n2455|| <code>mesh.workspace_replication</code> | Default true | Boolean |\n2456|| <code>mesh.payload_encryption</code> | Default <code>none</code> | Only <code>none</code> in v0.3.0 |\n2457|| <code>mesh.peers</code> | Default empty | Unique host ID and name; endpoint required |\n2458|| <code>mesh.peers[].ssh_args</code> | Default empty | Arg array; MUST NOT disable host-key checks |\n2459|| <code>mesh.peers[].workspace_roots</code> | Default empty | Unique logical roots within peer |\n2460|| <code>workspace_roots</code> | Default empty | At least one matching root required for workspace materialization |\n2461|| <code>providers.plugin_dirs</code> | Default empty | Absolute directories |\n2462|| <code>providers.allow_path_plugins</code> | Default true | Boolean |\n2463|| <code>providers.require_explicit_trust</code> | Default true | MUST remain true unless an enterprise policy supplies equivalent signed trust |\n2464|| <code>sync.chunk_bytes</code> | Default/fixed 4,194,304 | Protocol 1.0.0 constant |\n2465|| <code>sync.max_parallel_chunks</code> | Default 4 | Integer 1–32 |\n2466|| <code>sync.staging_retention_hours</code> | Default 72 | Integer 1–720 |\n2467|| <code>sync.tombstone_min_retention_days</code> | Default/minimum 90 | Integer 90–3,650 |\n2468|| <code>terminal.backend</code> | Platform default | <code>tmux</code> on macOS/Linux/WSL2; <code>conpty</code> on Windows |\n2469|| <code>terminal.safe_boundary_timeout_seconds</code> | Default 300 | Integer 1–3,600 |\n2470|| <code>terminal.graceful_stop_timeout_seconds</code> | Default 60 | Integer 1–600 |\n2471|| <code>service.enabled</code> | Default true after service installation | Boolean; false never disables core CLI |\n2472|| <code>service.health_interval_seconds</code> | Default 30 | Integer 5–3,600 |\n2473|| <code>restore.auto_resume</code> | Default false | Boolean; true still requires accepted provider/platform restore gate |\n2474|| <code>profiles.yolo.require_first_use_confirmation</code> | Default true | Boolean; non-interactive launch still requires explicit profile |\n2475|\n2476|Every TOML table and array-of-tables is closed. The allowed root members are\n2477|the five scalar keys in the example plus <code>mesh</code>,\n2478|<code>workspace_roots</code>, <code>providers</code>, <code>sync</code>,\n2479|<code>terminal</code>, <code>service</code>, <code>restore</code>, and\n2480|<code>profiles</code>. <code>mesh</code>, <code>providers</code>,\n2481|<code>sync</code>, <code>terminal</code>, <code>service</code>, and\n2482|<code>restore</code> contain exactly their dotted keys in the table above;\n2483|<code>profiles</code> contains exactly <code>yolo</code>, whose only key is\n2484|<code>require_first_use_confirmation</code>.\n2485|\n2486|Each <code>mesh.peers</code> entry contains exactly\n2487|<code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>name:string[1..64]</code>,\n2488|<code>endpoint:string[1..1024]</code>,\n2489|<code>platform:macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code>,\n2490|<code>ssh_args:array&lt;string&gt;[0..64]</code>, and\n2491|<code>workspace_roots:WorkspaceRoot[0..64]</code>. Each root-level or peer\n2492|WorkspaceRoot contains exactly <code>logical_root:string[1..64]</code> matching\n2493|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}</code> and <code>path:absolute-path</code>.\n2494|Endpoint and every SSH argument are passed as atomic argv values, never through\n2495|a shell. Each argument is 1–4,096 UTF-8 bytes, and the total SSH argv is at\n2496|most 65,536 bytes. Omitting a defaulted member uses the table's stated default;\n2497|explicit null is not a TOML value and is never accepted as a substitute.\n2498|\n2499|SSH arguments that set <code>StrictHostKeyChecking=no</code>, an empty\n2500|<code>UserKnownHostsFile</code>, or an equivalent host-authentication bypass\n2501|MUST fail configuration validation.\n2502|\n2503|### 6.4 Configuration 2.0.0 directory extension\n2504|\n2505|Configuration 2.0.0 retains all Configuration 1 members and replaces the\n2506|closed root/table registry with the directory-capable registry below. It is a\n2507|new major; a v1 reader MUST reject it, and a v2 binary MUST NOT write v1 syntax\n2508|after directory state exists.\n2509|\n2510|The v2 root adds exactly <code>directory</code>,\n2511|<code>directory_installations</code>,\n2512|<code>directory_enrichment_profiles</code>, and\n2513|<code>directory_peer_disclosure</code>. The closed <code>directory</code> table\n2514|contains exactly:\n2515|\n2516|| Key | Default/constraint |\n2517|| --- | --- |\n2518|| <code>enabled</code> | false; boolean |\n2519|| <code>mode</code> | <code>on_demand|service</code>; default on_demand |\n2520|| <code>scan_interval_seconds</code> | 300; uint53[5..86400] |\n2521|| <code>scan_debounce_seconds</code> | 5; uint53[0..3600] |\n2522|| <code>scan_concurrency</code> | 2; uint53[1..32] |\n2523|| <code>fresh_current_seconds</code> | 120; uint53[1..86400] |\n2524|| <code>fresh_aging_seconds</code> | 600; greater than current, at most 604800 |\n2525|| <code>fresh_stale_seconds</code> | 3600; greater than aging, at most 31536000 |\n2526|| <code>plan_expiry_seconds</code> | 300; uint53[30..3600] |\n2527|| <code>default_metadata_policy</code> | <code>local_only|mesh_sanitized|reference_only</code>; default local_only on upgrade and mesh_sanitized only for a newly initialized trusted mesh after explicit setup choice |\n2528|| <code>generated_summary_upgrade_choice</code> | <code>unset|local_only|mesh_sanitized|reference_only</code>; existing meshes require a non-unset choice before replication |\n2529|| <code>default_enrichment_profile_id</code> | digest or empty; empty means deterministic extraction only |\n2530|| <code>query_page_default</code>/<code>query_page_max</code> | 100/1000; positive and default no greater than max |\n2531|| <code>query_batch_max</code> | 64; uint53[1..64] |\n2532|| <code>grep_result_max</code> | 1000; uint53[1..10000] |\n2533|| <code>transcript_grep_enabled</code> | false; source-local only when true |\n2534|| <code>embedding_index</code> | <code>disabled|local_only</code>; default disabled |\n2535|| <code>observation_retention_days</code> | 365; uint53[30..3650] |\n2536|| <code>job_retention_days</code> | 180; uint53[30..3650] |\n2537|| <code>operation_retention_days</code> | 365; uint53[90..3650] |\n2538|| <code>provenance_compaction</code> | false; when true, only Section 10.8 provenance-preserving compaction is legal |\n2539|\n2540|Each <code>directory_installations</code> entry contains exactly\n2541|<code>installation_id:digest</code>, <code>environment_id:string[1..64]</code>,\n2542|<code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n2543|<code>adapter_id:string[1..64]</code>,\n2544|<code>scan_root_authority_ids:sorted unique digest[1..64]</code>,\n2545|<code>enabled:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. A root authority is\n2546|configured through a local opaque resolver; raw roots, auth-store paths, and\n2547|credentials are not serializable fields.\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c57f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07d5e-0f16-71a3-abaf-54c2f5d26492"},"sequence":282,"recorded_at":1780531400000559,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"856dbc62-e8b6-4fad-b436-ef1ae6eda625"},"task_id":"856dbc62-e8b6-4fad-b436-ef1ae6eda625","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"856dbc62-e8b6-4fad-b436-ef1ae6eda625"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c581","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07d5e-0f16-71a3-abaf-54c2f5d26492"},"sequence":283,"recorded_at":1780531400000561,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf"},"call_id":"call_01a07d5eadd975d0a65498a9e8898e25","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(2267 line(s) above)\n2268|### 5.7 Derived session states\n2269|\n2270|The state engine derives exactly one state for each\n2271|<code>(session_id, host_id)</code> projection and separately reports the\n2272|winning owner's projection as the session lifecycle state. Thus a destination\n2273|can be <code>running</code> while an old host is locally <code>stale</code>:\n2274|\n2275|| State | Meaning |\n2276|| --- | --- |\n2277|| <code>creating</code> | Session record and initial lease exist; no first validated checkpoint exists and bootstrap launch/retry is in progress |\n2278|| <code>running</code> | Winning owner has a live provider turn or accepts input |\n2279|| <code>idle</code> | Owner is live at an adapter-proven safe turn boundary |\n2280|| <code>quiescing</code> | New input is blocked while waiting for a safe boundary and clean stop |\n2281|| <code>checkpointing</code> | Safe state is being captured and validated |\n2282|| <code>stopped</code> | Winning owner has no provider process and a non-null validated checkpoint from which it is resumable |\n2283|| <code>materializing</code> | Destination staging/validation is in progress; it is not owner-active |\n2284|| <code>parked</code> | Wrapper exists but refuses provider launch due to remote/unknown ownership |\n2285|| <code>failed</code> | An operation failed and recovery metadata exists |\n2286|| <code>stale</code> | Local process/replica has a losing fencing token |\n2287|| <code>tombstoned</code> | Session is logically deleted and cannot resume |\n2288|\n2289|The exact <code>SessionState</code> enum is, in this order,\n2290|<code>creating</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>idle</code>,\n2291|<code>quiescing</code>, <code>checkpointing</code>, <code>stopped</code>,\n2292|<code>materializing</code>, <code>parked</code>, <code>failed</code>,\n2293|<code>stale</code>, and <code>tombstoned</code>. Every RPC and CLI field typed\n2294|<code>SessionState</code> uses exactly this registry. The spellings\n2295|<code>created</code>, <code>starting</code>, and <code>quiesced</code> are not\n2296|session lifecycle states in Session Record 1.0.0; a subsystem-specific bridge state\n2297|MAY use <code>quiesced</code> only where Section 9 declares that separate enum.\n2298|\n2299|Allowed transitions are:\n2300|\n2301|~~~text\n2302|creating -> running | idle | failed\n2303|running -> idle | quiescing | failed | stale\n2304|idle -> running | quiescing | checkpointing | stopped | stale\n2305|quiescing -> idle | checkpointing | failed | stale\n2306|checkpointing -> idle | stopped | materializing | failed\n2307|materializing -> stopped | running | parked | failed\n2308|stopped -> materializing | running | parked | tombstoned\n2309|parked -> materializing | running | stopped | stale\n2310|failed -> creating | stopped | parked | materializing | stale | tombstoned\n2311|stale -> stopped | tombstoned\n2312|~~~\n2313|\n2314|Any transition not listed MUST fail with <code>invalid_state_transition</code>.\n2315|Force takeover changes the old host's derived state to <code>stale</code> after\n2316|lease convergence even if its process remains alive.\n2317|\n2318|The <code>failed -> creating</code> edge is permitted only for an epoch-1\n2319|session with no validated checkpoint, the same winning create lease, no\n2320|authoritative <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event, and the Section 13.1\n2321|bootstrap-retry preconditions. A force-closed bootstrap remains\n2322|<code>failed</code> and non-resumable. No event or RPC result may derive\n2323|<code>stopped</code> while <code>newest_checkpoint_id</code> is null.\n2324|\n2325|## 6. Configuration contract\n2326|\n2327|### 6.1 Loading and precedence\n2328|\n2329|Configuration schema <code>urn:ax:schema:config</code> version\n2330|<code>1.0.0</code> is encoded as TOML. Precedence, highest first, is:\n2331|\n2332|1. command flags;\n2333|2. the five documented Section 3.2 <code>AX_*</code> path overrides;\n2334|3. values in the selected configuration file; and\n2335|4. normative defaults in this section.\n2336|\n2337|The configuration file itself is selected by <code>--config</code>, then\n2338|<code>AX_CONFIG</code>, then the platform-default configuration directory's\n2339|<code>config.toml</code>. The data, state, cache, and runtime overrides select\n2340|infrastructure roots and are not TOML field-by-field overrides. The same\n2341|resolved roots MUST be used by the CLI, service, RPC server, provider host, and\n2342|crash recovery for the entire process lifetime.\n2343|\n2344|Unknown top-level keys MUST fail configuration loading. Secret values MUST NOT\n2345|be accepted in config fields; a provider MAY name a machine-local environment\n2346|variable or credential profile.\n2347|\n2348|The complete 1.0.0 environment-override registry is\n2349|<code>AX_CONFIG</code>, <code>AX_DATA_DIR</code>,\n2350|<code>AX_STATE_DIR</code>, <code>AX_CACHE_DIR</code>, and\n2351|<code>AX_RUNTIME_DIR</code>, with the value kinds and empty-value rule in\n2352|Section 3.2. There are no other field-by-field <code>AX_*</code> overrides in\n2353|this version. Provider credential variables are destination-local inputs and\n2354|never configuration values.\n2355|\n2356|### 6.2 Normative example\n2357|\n2358|~~~toml\n2359|schema = \"urn:ax:schema:config\"\n2360|schema_version = \"1.0.0\"\n2361|host_id = \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\"\n2362|host_name = \"mbp-ivan\"\n2363|platform = \"macos\"\n2364|\n2365|[mesh]\n2366|transport = \"ssh\"\n2367|sync_interval_seconds = 60\n2368|connect_timeout_seconds = 10\n2369|rpc_timeout_seconds = 300\n2370|workspace_replication = true\n2371|payload_encryption = \"none\"\n2372|\n2373|[[mesh.peers]]\n2374|host_id = \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\"\n2375|name = \"workstation\"\n2376|endpoint = \"ivan@workstation.tailnet.ts.net\"\n2377|platform = \"linux\"\n2378|ssh_args = [\"-o\", \"BatchMode=yes\"]\n2379|\n2380|[[mesh.peers.workspace_roots]]\n2381|logical_root = \"relux\"\n2382|path = \"/srv/relux\"\n2383|\n2384|[[workspace_roots]]\n2385|logical_root = \"relux\"\n2386|path = \"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks\"\n2387|\n2388|[providers]\n2389|plugin_dirs = [\"/Users/iv/.local/libexec/ax/providers\"]\n2390|allow_path_plugins = true\n2391|require_explicit_trust = true\n2392|\n2393|[sync]\n2394|chunk_bytes = 4194304\n2395|max_parallel_chunks = 4\n2396|staging_retention_hours = 72\n2397|tombstone_min_retention_days = 90\n2398|\n2399|[terminal]\n2400|backend = \"tmux\"\n2401|safe_boundary_timeout_seconds = 300\n2402|graceful_stop_timeout_seconds = 60\n2403|\n2404|[service]\n2405|enabled = true\n2406|health_interval_seconds = 30\n2407|\n2408|[restore]\n2409|auto_resume = false\n2410|\n2411|[profiles.yolo]\n2412|require_first_use_confirmation = true\n2413|~~~\n2414|\n2415|On native Windows, a workspace mapping is written with a quoted TOML string\n2416|such as <code>path = \"D:\\\\Developer\\\\ReluxWorks\"</code>, and terminal backend\n2417|MUST be <code>conpty</code>. WSL2 configuration uses Linux paths and\n2418|<code>platform = \"wsl2\"</code>.\n2419|\n2420|### 6.3 Field constraints\n2421|\n2422|<code>platform</code> is one of <code>macos</code>, <code>linux</code>,\n2423|<code>wsl2</code>, or <code>windows</code>. A peer is authorized only when its\n2424|stable <code>host_id</code> appears in <code>mesh.peers</code> and the SSH\n2425|endpoint resolves to the authenticated host expected by SSH host-key policy.\n2426|Tailscale discovery MAY suggest a candidate configuration but MUST NOT write or\n2427|authorize it automatically.\n2428|\n2429|<code>mesh.payload_encryption</code> MUST be <code>none</code> in v0.3.0.\n2430|Other values MUST fail as unsupported. SSH supplies transport protection; this\n2431|setting prevents a misleading at-rest encryption claim.\n2432|\n2433|<code>sync.chunk_bytes</code> MUST equal 4,194,304 in Configuration 1.0.0.\n2434|Implementations MAY expose the field for forward compatibility but MUST reject\n2435|another value in this protocol version.\n2436|\n2437|Workspace roots MUST have unique <code>logical_root</code> values. Paths MAY\n2438|differ across hosts. A materializer MUST map a workspace using\n2439|<code>logical_root</code> plus a validated relative path, never a source\n2440|absolute path.\n2441|\n2442|The complete v1 field/default contract is:\n2443|\n2444|| Key | Required/default | Constraint |\n2445|| --- | --- | --- |\n2446|| <code>schema</code> | Required | Exact config schema identifier |\n2447|| <code>schema_version</code> | Required | Compatible version negotiated by this binary |\n2448|| <code>host_id</code> | Required | Stable UUIDv7; changing it creates a new mesh host |\n2449|| <code>host_name</code> | Required | 1–64 printable non-control UTF-8 characters |\n2450|| <code>platform</code> | Required | One of the four values above; MUST match runtime probe |\n2451|| <code>mesh.transport</code> | Default <code>ssh</code> | Only <code>ssh</code> in v0.3.0 |\n2452|| <code>mesh.sync_interval_seconds</code> | Default 60 | Integer 5–86,400 |\n2453|| <code>mesh.connect_timeout_seconds</code> | Default 10 | Integer 1–300 |\n2454|| <code>mesh.rpc_timeout_seconds</code> | Default 300 | Integer 10–3,600 |\n2455|| <code>mesh.workspace_replication</code> | Default true | Boolean |\n2456|| <code>mesh.payload_encryption</code> | Default <code>none</code> | Only <code>none</code> in v0.3.0 |\n2457|| <code>mesh.peers</code> | Default empty | Unique host ID and name; endpoint required |\n2458|| <code>mesh.peers[].ssh_args</code> | Default empty | Arg array; MUST NOT disable host-key checks |\n2459|| <code>mesh.peers[].workspace_roots</code> | Default empty | Unique logical roots within peer |\n2460|| <code>workspace_roots</code> | Default empty | At least one matching root required for workspace materialization |\n2461|| <code>providers.plugin_dirs</code> | Default empty | Absolute directories |\n2462|| <code>providers.allow_path_plugins</code> | Default true | Boolean |\n2463|| <code>providers.require_explicit_trust</code> | Default true | MUST remain true unless an enterprise policy supplies equivalent signed trust |\n2464|| <code>sync.chunk_bytes</code> | Default/fixed 4,194,304 | Protocol 1.0.0 constant |\n2465|| <code>sync.max_parallel_chunks</code> | Default 4 | Integer 1–32 |\n2466|| <code>sync.staging_retention_hours</code> | Default 72 | Integer 1–720 |\n2467|| <code>sync.tombstone_min_retention_days</code> | Default/minimum 90 | Integer 90–3,650 |\n2468|| <code>terminal.backend</code> | Platform default | <code>tmux</code> on macOS/Linux/WSL2; <code>conpty</code> on Windows |\n2469|| <code>terminal.safe_boundary_timeout_seconds</code> | Default 300 | Integer 1–3,600 |\n2470|| <code>terminal.graceful_stop_timeout_seconds</code> | Default 60 | Integer 1–600 |\n2471|| <code>service.enabled</code> | Default true after service installation | Boolean; false never disables core CLI |\n2472|| <code>service.health_interval_seconds</code> | Default 30 | Integer 5–3,600 |\n2473|| <code>restore.auto_resume</code> | Default false | Boolean; true still requires accepted provider/platform restore gate |\n2474|| <code>profiles.yolo.require_first_use_confirmation</code> | Default true | Boolean; non-interactive launch still requires explicit profile |\n2475|\n2476|Every TOML table and array-of-tables is closed. The allowed root members are\n2477|the five scalar keys in the example plus <code>mesh</code>,\n2478|<code>workspace_roots</code>, <code>providers</code>, <code>sync</code>,\n2479|<code>terminal</code>, <code>service</code>, <code>restore</code>, and\n2480|<code>profiles</code>. <code>mesh</code>, <code>providers</code>,\n2481|<code>sync</code>, <code>terminal</code>, <code>service</code>, and\n2482|<code>restore</code> contain exactly their dotted keys in the table above;\n2483|<code>profiles</code> contains exactly <code>yolo</code>, whose only key is\n2484|<code>require_first_use_confirmation</code>.\n2485|\n2486|Each <code>mesh.peers</code> entry contains exactly\n2487|<code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>name:string[1..64]</code>,\n2488|<code>endpoint:string[1..1024]</code>,\n2489|<code>platform:macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code>,\n2490|<code>ssh_args:array&lt;string&gt;[0..64]</code>, and\n2491|<code>workspace_roots:WorkspaceRoot[0..64]</code>. Each root-level or peer\n2492|WorkspaceRoot contains exactly <code>logical_root:string[1..64]</code> matching\n2493|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}</code> and <code>path:absolute-path</code>.\n2494|Endpoint and every SSH argument are passed as atomic argv values, never through\n2495|a shell. Each argument is 1–4,096 UTF-8 bytes, and the total SSH argv is at\n2496|most 65,536 bytes. Omitting a defaulted member uses the table's stated default;\n2497|explicit null is not a TOML value and is never accepted as a substitute.\n2498|\n2499|SSH arguments that set <code>StrictHostKeyChecking=no</code>, an empty\n2500|<code>UserKnownHostsFile</code>, or an equivalent host-authentication bypass\n2501|MUST fail configuration validation.\n2502|\n2503|### 6.4 Configuration 2.0.0 directory extension\n2504|\n2505|Configuration 2.0.0 retains all Configuration 1 members and replaces the\n2506|closed root/table registry with the directory-capable registry below. It is a\n2507|new major; a v1 reader MUST reject it, and a v2 binary MUST NOT write v1 syntax\n2508|after directory state exists.\n2509|\n2510|The v2 root adds exactly <code>directory</code>,\n2511|<code>directory_installations</code>,\n2512|<code>directory_enrichment_profiles</code>, and\n2513|<code>directory_peer_disclosure</code>. The closed <code>directory</code> table\n2514|contains exactly:\n2515|\n2516|| Key | Default/constraint |\n2517|| --- | --- |\n2518|| <code>enabled</code> | false; boolean |\n2519|| <code>mode</code> | <code>on_demand|service</code>; default on_demand |\n2520|| <code>scan_interval_seconds</code> | 300; uint53[5..86400] |\n2521|| <code>scan_debounce_seconds</code> | 5; uint53[0..3600] |\n2522|| <code>scan_concurrency</code> | 2; uint53[1..32] |\n2523|| <code>fresh_current_seconds</code> | 120; uint53[1..86400] |\n2524|| <code>fresh_aging_seconds</code> | 600; greater than current, at most 604800 |\n2525|| <code>fresh_stale_seconds</code> | 3600; greater than aging, at most 31536000 |\n2526|| <code>plan_expiry_seconds</code> | 300; uint53[30..3600] |\n2527|| <code>default_metadata_policy</code> | <code>local_only|mesh_sanitized|reference_only</code>; default local_only on upgrade and mesh_sanitized only for a newly initialized trusted mesh after explicit setup choice |\n2528|| <code>generated_summary_upgrade_choice</code> | <code>unset|local_only|mesh_sanitized|reference_only</code>; existing meshes require a non-unset choice before replication |\n2529|| <code>default_enrichment_profile_id</code> | digest or empty; empty means deterministic extraction only |\n2530|| <code>query_page_default</code>/<code>query_page_max</code> | 100/1000; positive and default no greater than max |\n2531|| <code>query_batch_max</code> | 64; uint53[1..64] |\n2532|| <code>grep_result_max</code> | 1000; uint53[1..10000] |\n2533|| <code>transcript_grep_enabled</code> | false; source-local only when true |\n2534|| <code>embedding_index</code> | <code>disabled|local_only</code>; default disabled |\n2535|| <code>observation_retention_days</code> | 365; uint53[30..3650] |\n2536|| <code>job_retention_days</code> | 180; uint53[30..3650] |\n2537|| <code>operation_retention_days</code> | 365; uint53[90..3650] |\n2538|| <code>provenance_compaction</code> | false; when true, only Section 10.8 provenance-preserving compaction is legal |\n2539|\n2540|Each <code>directory_installations</code> entry contains exactly\n2541|<code>installation_id:digest</code>, <code>environment_id:string[1..64]</code>,\n2542|<code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n2543|<code>adapter_id:string[1..64]</code>,\n2544|<code>scan_root_authority_ids:sorted unique digest[1..64]</code>,\n2545|<code>enabled:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. A root authority is\n2546|configured through a local opaque resolver; raw roots, auth-store paths, and\n2547|credentials are not serializable fields.\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
