{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e991","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07d5e-0f16-71a3-abaf-54c2f5d26492"},"sequence":4899,"recorded_at":1780531400009793,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"791fb340-3872-4137-9ab8-54c814d27952"},"task_id":"791fb340-3872-4137-9ab8-54c814d27952","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"791fb340-3872-4137-9ab8-54c814d27952","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 159-164\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## Stated bounds (not silent gaps)\n-\n-- No crash window: `Project` only reads; placing secconftest points\n-  around reads would measure nothing (leaf 1's lesson). The DoD crash\n-  item is therefore not claimed: idempotency is proven by purity\n-  (`TestReduceIsPure`, `TestProjectIsIdempotentAcrossReads`) instead.\n+## Stated bounds (not silent gaps)\n+\n+- Crash evidence lives in the owned durable window: the projector is\n+  read-only and owns no window of its own, so the secconftest points\n+  sit at the four `CreateSession` step boundaries (session-dir, record,\n+  events-dir, chain — one per boundary) and drive `Project`: faults at\n+  the first three derive the parked state with its exact retry, the\n+  identical retry heals into creating, and a fault past the chain\n+  derives creating with a session-exists refusal on retry. Purity pins\n+  idempotency on top (`TestReduceIsPure`,\n+  `TestProjectIsIdempotentAcrossReads`). No decorative points around\n+  reads were added (leaf 1's lesson).\n"}}}
