{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ebd1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07d5e-0f16-71a3-abaf-54c2f5d26492"},"sequence":5187,"recorded_at":1780531400010369,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e2cea5ab-c4ff-4757-bfdf-44257ee82bbf"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Work handed off to review — `TASK-260830-1r9wrr` is `to-review`, checklist 21/21, both outcome artifacts attached.\n\nWhat was delivered: new `internal/sessstate` package (14 files, +4823/−0) deriving all 11 `SessionState` values, winning-epoch resolution with five named conflict rules, current checkpoints, provider identity, and terminal binding (v1 + v4) — plus a README section and logbook entry. `sessrepo` and `provhost` production untouched.\n\nEvidence: AC coverage 10/10 with production call sites; all gates green (build, vet, Windows vet/build, gofmt, tracecheck, full suite, race over all 25 packages in 4 groups, 91.7% cover, cigate selections); three invcore censuses (67 refusal sites, 11 states, 24 event types, alias/var/dot-import/shadow plants); mutation battery 26 applied / 26 killed / 0 survived with narrowing/arm-deletion/census-test/audit-only separate plus NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL controls; candidate tree `95b2f9e58f00ee9aea5aba32c548bcc1e44e5a34` with exactly the 16 CR paths enumerated.\n\nTwo findings worth knowing: the repo-wide suite caught my decode re-verifying blobs, which the provhost gate forbids outside `sessrepo` — decode now projects members from attested bytes instead. And the crash checklist item is covered through secconftest points at all four create-step boundaries driving `Project` (fault→parked→retry heals, asserted in-test), since the read-only projector owns no durable window of its own.","reason":null}}
